 "notes": "ALP-photon cosmological (BBN + Planck Neff) exclusion. Curve = solid blue boundary of the excluded region in Fig. 6 right panel (neff_opt_gphi.pdf), i.e. the robust case (iii): combined 95% CL BBN bound allowing simultaneous variation of both Delta-Neff and neutrino chemical potential xi_nue (maximal cancellation of bounds). This is the paper headline robust constraint (title + Sec.6 conclusion: significant and robust constraints remain even under maximal tuning; main results per text are figs 5 and 6). The plot is already in the paper native g_phi-gamma [1/GeV], which is identical to the canonical g_agamma (eq. 2.1: L = -(g_phigamma/4) phi F Ftilde), so no conversion applied; mass converted MeV->eV (x1e6). Extracted by vector-drawing color/dash matching (blue solid dashes=[]), axes calibrated from frame+tick strokes (x:63.6px=1e-2 MeV..322.8px=1e3 MeV, 51.84px/dec; y:269.2px=1e-11..19.2px=1e-3, 31.25px/dec); cross-checked via eq.2.2 tau=64pi/(m^3 g^2): m=1GeV,g=2.7e-11 -> tau~0.18s (BBN onset). Boundary: near-vertical low-mass cutoff at m~0.30 MeV (first pts, g from 1e-3 frame-cap down to ~1.1e-6) then monotonic descent to (1e3 MeV, 2.7e-11). Excluded region lies above/left of this curve. Alternative stronger curves in same panel: standard cosmology (blue dashed) and +Delta-Neff only (blue dash-dotted); not reported. Not a DM search (density-independent).",
